al sentiment against the  nicaraguans and we will use these  members of the journalistic community as  our pawns  to achieve that political end  and they were building off of something  that had happened  in nicaragua under samosa where samosa's  national guard killed a united states  journalist just murdered him on the  street  and the american people turned against  samosa so they said hey that's the  scenario let's kill american journalists  make them think the sandinistas did it  and turn them against  against the sanonises well if any  community in this country has a stake in  what we're doing it's the journalistic  community and if there ever was a time  here we are in the 200th anniversary of  the united states constitution  we're looking at the press the free  press the first amendment and a direct  attack upon them that threatens their  ability to gather news without becoming  targets  it's a perfect time for them to step  forward and say okay we're going to be  embraced by the constitution and we're  going to embrace the constitution we're  going to tell you the truth about what's  going on in this country in the world so  that you can use the constitutional  system to make it right so you can be an  informed electorate giving your informed  consent to policies that are going on  and not have any policies going on that  don't have your informed consent i might  note that the kristak institute has  published an affidavit of daniel sheehan  who's one of the members of your group  that gives all the information on the  show  that we've covered today that goes into  the whole history basically  it basically tells what it is we know  and how we came to know it and it's  available to the public how can  people get in touch with the chris deck  institute and find out about your work  and the information that you have we're  in washington dc the address there if  folks want to write is 1324  north capitol street in washington d.c  and the zip is two triple zero tw